{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2139\ufe0f] [2026-02-06 07:52:21 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-StructureMap] [Project: scribe_pro_cleanup] Server.py analysis complete. Entry point uses sys.path manipulation to add parent directory, imports from scribe_mcp package, and creates global singletons (app, state_manager, storage_backend, router_context_manager). MCP SDK is optional with fallback stubs. Key import pattern: 'from scribe_mcp.X.Y import Z' - all absolute imports from package root. | entry_point=server.py; global_singletons=[\"app (Server instance)\", \"state_manager (StateManager)\", \"storage_backend\", \"router_context_manager\", \"agent_context_manager\", \"agent_identity\"]; import_pattern=absolute from scribe_mcp.*; mcp_optional=True; reasoning={\"how\": \"Read server.py structure and import statements, verified import patterns\", \"what\": \"Identified sys.path manipulation, singleton pattern, and absolute import convention\", \"why\": \"Entry point behavior determines how module resolution works in production\"}; sys_path_hack=adds parent dir to sys.path at line 14-18; priority=low; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_pro_cleanup/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-02-06T07:52:21.750696+00:00_0fb84907", "timestamp": "2026-02-06T07:52:21.750763+00:00"}
