{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2139\ufe0f] [2026-02-06 07:52:22 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-StartupPerf] [Project: scribe_pro_cleanup] Traced complete startup sequence from server.py. Key findings: (1) Module-level initialization creates StateManager, storage_backend via create_storage_backend(), and RouterContextManager immediately on import - these are EAGER. (2) _startup() async function performs: storage setup, old entry cleanup, plugin initialization, bridge registry initialization + manifest discovery + activation, agent context initialization, legacy state migration, session cleanup task, bridge tool registration, journal replay background task. (3) All import-time creation happens before any request served. | confidence=0.95; reasoning={\"how\": \"Read server.py top-to-bottom, traced import statements and _startup() function\", \"what\": \"Identified module-level (import-time) vs startup-time initialization patterns\", \"why\": \"Need to understand what's blocking at startup vs what can be deferred\"}; startup_bottlenecks=[\"storage_backend creation at module level\", \"StateManager creation at module level\", \"storage.setup() in _startup\", \"cleanup_old_entries() in _startup\", \"plugin initialization in _startup\", \"bridge discovery/activation in _startup\"]; priority=low; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_pro_cleanup/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-02-06T07:52:22.545615+00:00_c40579c8", "timestamp": "2026-02-06T07:52:22.545712+00:00"}
