{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2139\ufe0f] [2026-02-06 07:52:32 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-Security] [Project: scribe_pro_cleanup] Starting comprehensive security audit. Will investigate: SQL injection risks (storage/sqlite.py, postgres.py), path traversal vulnerabilities (read_file, edit_file, search), hardcoded secrets, input validation across all MCP tools, dependency vulnerabilities, file permission issues, error information leakage, authentication/authorization gaps, unsafe deserialization, and log injection risks. This is a production MCP server handling file operations and database access - security issues could expose user data or enable attacks. | agent=research; audit_type=security; priority=low; reasoning={\"how\": \"Systematic code review using scribe.search for patterns and scribe.read_file for detailed analysis, with findings logged and documented\", \"what\": \"10 security domains to investigate: SQL injection, path traversal, secrets, input validation, dependencies, file permissions, error leakage, auth, deserialization, log injection\", \"why\": \"Production MCP server requires comprehensive security audit before deployment - potential for data exposure, path traversal, and injection attacks\"}; scope=full_codebase; stage=research; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_pro_cleanup/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-02-06T07:52:32.861525+00:00_8adad248", "timestamp": "2026-02-06T07:52:32.861608+00:00"}
