{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2705] [2026-02-06 07:53:00 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-StartupPerf] [Project: scribe_pro_cleanup] Analyzed module-level initialization overhead. FINDING: Both SQLiteStorage and StateManager have lightweight __init__ methods - no heavy I/O at import time. SQLiteStorage defers DB connection to setup(), StateManager defers file reading to load(). This is GOOD DESIGN - no blocking work at module import. The bottleneck is NOT in the constructors themselves. | confidence=0.95; finding=No heavy work in constructors - initialization properly deferred; reasoning={\"how\": \"Read constructor code - both use lazy initialization pattern\", \"what\": \"Checked __init__ methods of StateManager and SQLiteStorage for synchronous I/O\", \"why\": \"Need to determine if module-level object creation blocks startup\"}; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_pro_cleanup/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-02-06T07:53:00.187630+00:00_361d2834", "timestamp": "2026-02-06T07:53:00.187694+00:00"}
