{"op": "append", "content": "[\u26a0\ufe0f] [2026-02-06 07:53:20 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-Security] [Project: scribe_pro_cleanup] SQL INJECTION FINDING #1: query_entries() method (lines 622-701) uses f-string interpolation for WHERE clause construction (line 669-675). While individual clauses use parameterized values, the dynamic construction pattern is fragile. The placeholders are correctly built from safe iterators (lines 652-659), but this pattern should be audited for safety. Current assessment: SAFE but fragile - relies on controlled clause construction without user-controlled SQL fragments. | agent=research; confidence=0.8; file=storage/sqlite.py; finding_type=sql_injection; lines=622-701; reasoning={\"how\": \"Code review of query_entries showing WHERE clause built from controlled clauses list with proper parameterization - no user-controlled SQL fragments detected\", \"what\": \"f-string WHERE clause interpolation pattern examined - clause building uses safe placeholder generation from controlled iterators, all values parameterized\", \"why\": \"Dynamic SQL construction requires careful review to ensure no injection vectors exist\"}; severity=low; stage=research; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_pro_cleanup/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-02-06T07:53:20.301575+00:00_864890b3", "timestamp": "2026-02-06T07:53:20.301642+00:00"}
