{"op": "append", "content": "[\u26a0\ufe0f] [2026-02-06 07:53:29 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-StructureMap] [Project: scribe_pro_cleanup] Path resolution analysis complete. Found 50+ instances of __file__ usage for path resolution. CRITICAL FRAGILE POINTS: server.py line 16 (_REPO_ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent), config/settings.py line 220 (_default_root uses parents[1]), template_engine/engine.py line 36 (templates folder), utils/reminder_monitoring.py line 31 (SCRIBE_ROOT). All these will break in src/ layout where depth changes. | __file___usage_count=50; critical_breakage_points=[\"server.py:16 (_REPO_ROOT = parent.parent)\", \"config/settings.py:220 (parents[1])\", \"template_engine/engine.py:36 (parent.parent/templates)\", \"utils/reminder_monitoring.py:31 (parent.parent)\"]; migration_requirement=ALL __file__-based paths must be refactored to use importlib.resources or package-relative paths; reasoning={\"how\": \"Searched for __file__ pattern, analyzed context in server.py, config/settings.py, template_engine, utils\", \"what\": \"Identified 50+ instances, cataloged critical breakage points where depth assumptions are hardcoded\", \"why\": \"Path resolution using __file__ and parent traversal is the #1 cause of src/ migration failures\"}; risk_level=HIGH; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_pro_cleanup/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-02-06T07:53:29.334503+00:00_1eed2313", "timestamp": "2026-02-06T07:53:29.334570+00:00"}
