{"op": "append", "content": "[\u26a0\ufe0f] [2026-02-06 07:53:40 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-StartupPerf] [Project: scribe_pro_cleanup] Identified MAJOR startup bottleneck: _initialise() method in SQLiteStorage is 631 lines (lines 849-1480). Contains: (1) CREATE TABLE statements for 20+ tables, (2) CREATE INDEX for 30+ indexes, (3) Multiple column migrations using _ensure_column (each does PRAGMA table_info check), (4) Data backfill migrations. ALL of this runs synchronously at startup via await storage_backend.setup() in server._startup(). THEN cleanup_old_entries() runs another DB query. This is the primary blocking operation. | confidence=0.98; critical_finding=Database initialization is synchronous and comprehensive; reasoning={\"how\": \"Read sqlite.py _initialise method, counted operations, identified blocking I/O patterns\", \"what\": \"Traced _initialise() - found 631 lines of schema creation, migrations, and backfills running on every startup\", \"why\": \"Need to understand what's blocking in storage initialization\"}; startup_cost_estimate=CREATE IF NOT EXISTS for 20+ tables + 30+ indexes + column checks + migrations; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_pro_cleanup/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-02-06T07:53:40.339490+00:00_5a8fb137", "timestamp": "2026-02-06T07:53:40.339574+00:00"}
