{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2705] [2026-02-06 07:53:54 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-Security] [Project: scribe_pro_cleanup] SQL INJECTION AUDIT COMPLETE - storage layer uses proper parameterization throughout. SQLite uses ? placeholders, Postgres uses $N placeholders. All user input is properly parameterized. Dynamic WHERE clause construction in query_entries() is safe (controlled clause building). No f-string SQL with user input detected. FINDING: SECURE - no SQL injection vulnerabilities found in database layer. | agent=research; confidence=0.95; files_audited=[\"storage/sqlite.py\", \"storage/postgres.py\", \"db/ops.py\"]; finding_type=sql_injection; reasoning={\"how\": \"Searched for SQL patterns, reviewed query_entries/insert_entry/upsert_project methods, verified no f-string SQL with user input\", \"what\": \"Reviewed all database query methods across SQLite and Postgres backends - all queries use parameterized placeholders (? for SQLite, $N for Postgres), dynamic WHERE clause construction uses safe placeholder generation\", \"why\": \"SQL injection is critical security vulnerability requiring comprehensive audit of all database queries\"}; severity=none; stage=research; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_pro_cleanup/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-02-06T07:53:54.271616+00:00_778efce5", "timestamp": "2026-02-06T07:53:54.271702+00:00"}
