{"op": "append", "content": "[\u26a0\ufe0f] [2026-02-06 07:54:26 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-StartupPerf] [Project: scribe_pro_cleanup] Analyzed import graphs of tool modules. FINDING: Heavy cross-dependencies create import cascade. Example: append_entry.py has 50+ import lines pulling in: BulkProcessor, estimator, agent_project_utils, reminders, files, time, sentinel_logs, logging_utils, log_enums, parameter_validator, config_manager, error_handler, security.sandbox, formatters. Each tool pulls similar dependency trees. When `from scribe_mcp import tools` runs, Python must load ALL these modules transitively. This compounds the startup delay. | confidence=0.95; import_cascade_depth=3-4 levels deep; reasoning={\"how\": \"Read import sections of append_entry.py and checked formatter dependencies\", \"what\": \"Traced import dependencies of individual tool modules - found heavy cross-module coupling\", \"why\": \"Need to understand import overhead beyond just tool count\"}; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_pro_cleanup/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-02-06T07:54:26.615029+00:00_cf2df6ef", "timestamp": "2026-02-06T07:54:26.615107+00:00"}
