{"op": "append", "content": "[\u26a0\ufe0f] [2026-02-06 07:54:38 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-DatabaseAudit] [Project: scribe_pro_cleanup] state.json audit complete and Postgres implementation assessed. FINDINGS: state.json (326KB, 5554 lines) is DEPRECATED but still actively used by StateManager class (state/manager.py lines 84-260). Contains project metadata, session state, agent state. StateManager has load() and save() methods that read/write JSON. Postgres implementation exists (storage/postgres.py, 260 lines, 18 methods) but is INCOMPLETE - missing many methods vs SQLite (SQLite has 30+ tables, Postgres implementation only has basic CRUD). NO connection pooling for Postgres (asyncpg needed). RISK: state.json and database have overlapping concerns creating dual-source-of-truth problem. | dual_state_risk=True; missing_postgres_features=[\"connection_pooling\", \"many_advanced_tables\", \"FTS5_search\", \"migration_tracking\", \"session_management\"]; postgres_completeness=~40%; reasoning={\"how\": \"Read state.json structure, traced StateManager code in state/manager.py, compared Postgres storage/postgres.py (260 lines, 18 methods) vs SQLite storage/sqlite.py (3050 lines, 50+ methods)\", \"what\": \"state.json is 326KB actively managed by StateManager despite being 'deprecated', Postgres exists but missing ~50% of SQLite features including connection pooling, dual state management creates consistency risks\", \"why\": \"Need to understand state.json usage and Postgres readiness to plan migration and consolidation\"}; state_json_status=deprecated_but_active; state_manager_lines=260; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_pro_cleanup/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-02-06T07:54:38.120716+00:00_3ad6d11e", "timestamp": "2026-02-06T07:54:38.120782+00:00"}
