{"op": "append", "content": "[\u274c] [2026-02-06 07:54:42 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-Security] [Project: scribe_pro_cleanup] PATH TRAVERSAL VULNERABILITY FOUND: read_file.py lines 1754-1760 uses Path.resolve() which follows symlinks BEFORE boundary enforcement at line 1821. Attack vector: Create symlink inside repo pointing to /etc/passwd, read_file will resolve symlink target and check if RESOLVED path is in repo (it won't be, will fail) BUT if symlink points to allowlisted absolute path, it bypasses repo boundary. Severity: MEDIUM - requires allow_outside_repo=True or allowlist manipulation, but symlink resolution should happen AFTER boundary checks, not before. | agent=research; confidence=0.85; cve_potential=medium; file=tools/read_file.py; finding_type=path_traversal; lines=1754-1760; reasoning={\"how\": \"Code review showing resolve() at lines 1756/1758 before policy enforcement at 1821 - resolved path checked against boundaries, not original path\", \"what\": \"Path.resolve() follows symlinks before _enforce_path_policy checks boundaries - attack requires symlink inside repo + allow_outside_repo flag or allowlist entry\", \"why\": \"Symlink resolution before boundary enforcement can allow reads outside intended scope\"}; severity=medium; stage=research; priority=high; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_pro_cleanup/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-02-06T07:54:42.666473+00:00_3e95b42e", "timestamp": "2026-02-06T07:54:42.666553+00:00"}
