{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2705] [2026-02-06 07:54:52 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-DatabaseAudit] [Project: scribe_pro_cleanup] Database architecture investigation complete. POSITIVE FINDINGS: SQLite has connection pooling (storage/pool.py, 409 lines, SQLiteConnectionPool with min=1, max=3, timeout handling, connection validation). StorageBackend abstraction is clean (storage/base.py, 400 lines, 30+ abstract methods). Schema migration system exists (_ensure_column, _ensure_index, scribe_migrations tracking table). COMPREHENSIVE SCHEMA: 30+ tables covering projects, entries, metrics, sessions, planning, document management, telemetry, bridges, FTS5 full-text search with triggers. Ready to compile full audit report. | positive_findings=[\"sqlite_connection_pool_exists\", \"clean_storage_abstraction\", \"migration_system_present\", \"comprehensive_schema\", \"fts5_search_implemented\"]; readiness_for_postgres=infrastructure_ready_but_incomplete_implementation; reasoning={\"how\": \"Read storage/pool.py for connection pooling implementation, reviewed base.py for abstraction quality, confirmed migration infrastructure exists\", \"what\": \"Connection pooling exists for SQLite (min=1 max=3), StorageBackend provides good abstraction layer, comprehensive schema with migrations support, all prerequisites for Postgres migration present\", \"why\": \"Need complete picture of database infrastructure before making consolidation/migration recommendations\"}; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_pro_cleanup/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-02-06T07:54:52.576688+00:00_833ca95f", "timestamp": "2026-02-06T07:54:52.576764+00:00"}
