{"op": "append", "content": "[\u274c] [2026-02-06 07:55:02 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-Security] [Project: scribe_pro_cleanup] PATH TRAVERSAL VULNERABILITY CONFIRMED IN 3 TOOLS: edit_file.py (lines 215/217), search.py (lines 651/653), and read_file.py (lines 1756/1758) ALL use Path.resolve() before boundary enforcement. This is a systemic pattern across file operation tools. FIX REQUIRED: Check symlinks BEFORE resolution, reject symlinks that point outside repo, OR check both original and resolved paths against boundaries. Priority: HIGH - affects all file operations. | agent=research; confidence=0.9; files=[\"tools/read_file.py\", \"tools/edit_file.py\", \"tools/search.py\"]; finding_type=path_traversal; pattern=systemic; reasoning={\"how\": \"Reviewed all file operation tools, identified identical resolve-before-check pattern in all three\", \"what\": \"All three file tools (read/edit/search) resolve symlinks before boundary checks - consistent pattern indicates architectural issue requiring coordinated fix\", \"why\": \"Systemic vulnerability across all file operation tools creates significant attack surface\"}; severity=high; stage=research; priority=high; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_pro_cleanup/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-02-06T07:55:02.917514+00:00_d84f334c", "timestamp": "2026-02-06T07:55:02.917576+00:00"}
