{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2139\ufe0f] [2026-02-06 07:55:51 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-CodeQuality] [Project: scribe_pro_cleanup] Code quality patterns audit - Phase 1 complete. Error handling: (1) Bare except: found in 6 files (entry.py, list_projects, set_project, query_entries, manage_docs, read_file) with 14 occurrences, (2) except Exception: found in reminders.py (8x) and server.py (2x) - 172 total matches. Naming: CamelCase classes correctly used (reminders.py, plugins/). Type hints: Mixed coverage - some files have return types (reminders.py, plugins/registry.py, utils/ modules), many tool files lack type hints. Config management: Well-organized hierarchy - config/ has .py modules + .json data files, .scribe/config/ has YAML for runtime config (scribe.yaml, boundary_rules.yaml, bridges/). .gitignore: Comprehensive but files still committed - Zone.Identifier, tmp_tests/, preflight .bak files all have ignore rules but exist in repo. Git ignore rules not retroactive. | audit_phase=code_patterns_phase1; config_management={\"formats\": [\".py\", \".json\", \".yaml\"], \"locations\": [\"config/\", \".scribe/config/\"], \"structure\": \"hierarchical\"}; error_handling={\"bare_except_count\": 14, \"bare_except_files\": 6, \"broad_exception_count\": 172, \"broad_exception_files\": 2}; gitignore_gap=rules exist but files committed - need retroactive cleanup; naming_conventions={\"consistency\": \"good\", \"pattern\": \"snake_case_functions_CamelCase_classes\"}; reasoning={\"how\": \"Used scribe.search for regex pattern matching across Python files, examined config directory structure, analyzed .gitignore rules vs actual files\", \"what\": \"Examined error handling anti-patterns, naming conventions, type hint coverage, config organization, gitignore effectiveness\", \"why\": \"Identify code quality patterns to establish cleanup and standardization priorities\"}; type_hints={\"coverage\": \"mixed\", \"missing_types\": [\"tools/\"], \"well_typed\": [\"reminders.py\", \"plugins/\", \"utils/\"]}; priority=low; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_pro_cleanup/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-02-06T07:55:51.658404+00:00_37ef1bfc", "timestamp": "2026-02-06T07:55:51.658477+00:00"}
