{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2139\ufe0f] [2026-02-06 07:56:17 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-CodeQuality] [Project: scribe_pro_cleanup] Module organization audit complete. Found 2 god modules: (1) storage/sqlite.py - 3,050 lines, 79 methods, single SQLiteStorage class handles ALL database operations (projects, entries, queries, migrations, sessions, vector indexing, document tracking), (2) tools/manage_docs.py - 3,410 lines, 29+ functions, handles create/edit/validate/search/batch operations. Good decomposition: utils/formatters/ was split from monolithic 2,934-line ResponseFormatter into 7 specialized modules (base, entry, file, project, ui, dispatcher) - clean separation of concerns. README is current (v2.2 documented). Config hierarchy is well-organized (config/ for static, .scribe/config/ for runtime). Overall: Good architecture with 2 notable god modules that handle complex domains but are difficult to navigate/maintain. | audit_phase=module_organization; god_modules=[{\"concerns\": [\"projects\", \"entries\", \"queries\", \"migrations\", \"sessions\", \"vector_indexing\", \"documents\"], \"file\": \"storage/sqlite.py\", \"lines\": 3050, \"methods\": 79}, {\"concerns\": [\"create\", \"edit\", \"validate\", \"search\", \"batch\"], \"file\": \"tools/manage_docs.py\", \"functions\": 29, \"lines\": 3410}]; good_decomposition={\"after\": \"7 specialized modules\", \"before\": \"2934 lines monolithic\", \"example\": \"utils/formatters/\"}; readme_status=current_v2.2; reasoning={\"how\": \"Used scribe.read_file scan_only mode to analyze structure without reading full content\", \"what\": \"Examined file sizes, class/function counts, separation of concerns, recent decomposition work\", \"why\": \"Identify module organization quality to plan refactoring priorities\"}; priority=low; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_pro_cleanup/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-02-06T07:56:17.944638+0