{"op": "append", "content": "[\u26a0\ufe0f] [2026-02-06 07:56:21 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-Security] [Project: scribe_pro_cleanup] DEPENDENCY AUDIT - Found 11 direct dependencies with version pinning using >= (minimum versions specified). Dependencies: asyncpg, jinja2, mcp, psutil, rich, pytest, pytest-asyncio, portalocker, pyyaml, watchdog, tiktoken, faiss-cpu, sentence-transformers, numpy. ISSUE: Using >= allows ANY newer version - should use ~= for patch-level updates or pin exact versions for production. Recommendation: Pin exact versions or use dependency scanning tools (pip-audit, safety) to check for known CVEs. FINDING: MEDIUM RISK - unpinned versions could introduce vulnerabilities. | agent=research; confidence=0.85; dependency_count=11; finding_type=dependency_vulnerability; pinning_strategy=minimum_version_only; reasoning={\"how\": \"Reviewed requirements.txt - found minimum version constraints only, no lockfile or exact version pinning\", \"what\": \"All dependencies use >= operator allowing unrestricted version upgrades - no upper bounds or exact version pins for production deployment\", \"why\": \"Unpinned dependencies can introduce security vulnerabilities through automatic updates\"}; severity=medium; stage=research; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_pro_cleanup/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-02-06T07:56:21.578768+00:00_34cdf740", "timestamp": "2026-02-06T07:56:21.578831+00:00"}
