{"op": "append", "content": "[\u26a0\ufe0f] [2026-02-06 07:56:43 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-Security] [Project: scribe_pro_cleanup] FILE PERMISSIONS & ERROR LEAKAGE AUDIT - ISSUE FOUND: set_project.py writes debug log to /tmp/scribe_session_debug.log without permission restrictions (world-readable by default on Unix). Contains session IDs and project names. Error handling generally safe - broad except Exception catches prevent stack trace leaks to clients. Recommendation: Set explicit file permissions (0o600) for temp files or write to user-specific directory. FINDING: LOW RISK - debug log exposure in multi-user systems. | agent=research; confidence=0.8; file=tools/set_project.py; finding_type=file_permissions; issue=world_readable_temp_file; lines=521-528; reasoning={\"how\": \"Code review of file write operations found /tmp write without permission restrictions\", \"what\": \"Debug log written to /tmp without explicit permissions - contains session IDs and project names, world-readable on Unix systems\", \"why\": \"Temp files with sensitive data need permission controls in multi-user environments\"}; severity=low; stage=research; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_pro_cleanup/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-02-06T07:56:43.465854+00:00_a3b4b622", "timestamp": "2026-02-06T07:56:43.465923+00:00"}
