{"op": "append", "content": "[\u26a0\ufe0f] [2026-02-06 07:56:57 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-Security] [Project: scribe_pro_cleanup] AUTHENTICATION & AUTHORIZATION AUDIT COMPLETE - MCP server has NO authentication or authorization layer. Any client connecting via stdio can use ALL tools without restrictions. No rate limiting detected. This is typical for local MCP servers (trust client = Claude Desktop), but represents significant risk if exposed over network or in multi-user environments. Recommendation: Document that server MUST NOT be exposed over network, add optional auth layer for network deployments, implement rate limiting for abuse prevention. FINDING: HIGH RISK if network-exposed, acceptable for local stdio-only deployment. | agent=research; confidence=0.95; deployment_model=stdio_only_safe; finding_type=authentication; reasoning={\"how\": \"Reviewed server.py and tool registration - no auth decorators, token verification, or access control found\", \"what\": \"No authentication, authorization, or rate limiting detected - MCP server trusts all clients via stdio transport\", \"why\": \"Lack of authentication allows unrestricted access - critical for network deployments\"}; severity=high_if_network_exposed; stage=research; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_pro_cleanup/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-02-06T07:56:57.540192+00:00_6597b1ea", "timestamp": "2026-02-06T07:56:57.540295+00:00"}
