{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2705] [2026-02-06 07:57:16 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-StderrAudit] [Project: scribe_pro_cleanup] Research document RESEARCH_STDERR_AUDIT_20260206_0755.md created successfully. Comprehensive audit complete with 115+ print() statements catalogued, categorized by severity and purpose, with detailed recommendations for centralized logging config, conditional startup noise, and proper error handling. Document includes implementation priority, testing strategy, and handoff notes for Architect. | confidence=0.95; deliverable=RESEARCH_STDERR_AUDIT_20260206_0755.md; estimated_effort=4-6 hours; key_findings=[\"server.py startup emits 35+ messages (HIGH priority)\", \"No centralized logging config (HIGH priority)\", \"Tool errors use print() not logging (MEDIUM priority)\", \"tiktoken warning on every startup (LOW priority)\"]; reasoning={\"how\": \"Systematic search across entire codebase using scribe.search and scribe.read_file, quantified every source, analyzed purpose, created implementation plan\", \"what\": \"Identified and categorized 115+ print statements, 3 stderr writes, 34 logging files without config, 2 warnings. Created actionable recommendations with priority levels.\", \"why\": \"Complete audit of all stderr/logging noise required for professional production operation\"}; recommendations=[\"Add centralized logging setup with SCRIBE_LOG_LEVEL env var\", \"Convert server.py startup to logging.info/warning/error\", \"Convert tool print() to proper logging\", \"Remove tiktoken warning\"]; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_pro_cleanup/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-02-06T07:57:16.022315+00:00_9a83575e", "timestamp": "2026-02-06T07:57:16.022388+00:00"}
