{"op": "append", "content": "[\u274c] [2026-02-06 07:58:41 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-Security] [Project: scribe_pro_cleanup] LOG INJECTION AUDIT - VULNERABILITY FOUND: compose_log_line() (shared/logging_utils.py lines 581-607) directly concatenates user input (message, agent, project_name) into log lines without sanitization. Attack vector: User provides message with newline characters, creates fake log entries. Example: message='Legit entry\\n[\u2705] [2026-01-01T00:00:00Z] [Agent: Attacker] [Project: fake] Injected fake entry'. Severity: MEDIUM - allows log forgery, can hide malicious activity, confuse log parsers. Recommendation: Strip/escape newlines and control characters from user input before logging. | agent=research; attack_vector=newline_injection; confidence=0.9; file=shared/logging_utils.py; finding_type=log_injection; lines=581-607; reasoning={\"how\": \"Code review of compose_log_line showing direct string concatenation without input sanitization\", \"what\": \"User input (message, agent, project_name) concatenated into log lines without sanitizing newlines or control characters - allows multi-line injection\", \"why\": \"Log injection allows attackers to forge log entries and hide malicious activity\"}; severity=medium; stage=research; priority=high; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_pro_cleanup/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-02-06T07:58:41.658387+00:00_fa0e0fee", "timestamp": "2026-02-06T07:58:41.658458+00:00"}
